  "work": {
    "abstract_text": "We give an alternative proof extending Kang's (2026) refutation of Yang–Chu–Zhang (2015), Conjecture 1(ii), p. 15. For its digamma remainder family G_a, we prove G_a''(1/64)>0 for every a>=331467377585/629168992256, and G_a''(1/64)>1 for every a>=5269/10000. These bounds exclude complete monotonicity of -G_a on a parameter half-line containing strictly interior points of the conjectured range. We also give a necessary positive constant-coefficient condition in the authors' Problem 1 and characterize all its degree-four solutions as positive multiples of the function in their Theorem 4 at its endpoint.",
